<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via over-the-weekend system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via over-the-weekend system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added reserves into the banking system via a round of over the weekend system repurchase agreements on Friday, a New York Fed spokeswoman confirmed.</p>
<p>The operation was mostly unexpected, given the soft federal funds rate and 14-day fixed system RPs operation done Thursday.</p>
<p>Fed funds opened at 5-1/8 percent, below the 5-1/4 percent target rate, but edged up to 5-3/16 percent at the Fed's intervention period.</p>
<p>(( -- Steven Scheer, N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1867))</p>
